on duration.\n2.  **Gap Contribution:** Directly addresses class specificity. Identifies PTZ as high risk. Suggests duration matters. Does not meet the \"2 studies\" criterion alone (needs one more).\n3.  **Remaining Gap:** Need another study to confirm these class-specific findings (external validation). Need to know if other classes are truly \"safe\" (some had small sample sizes).\n4.  **Action:** Search for another study comparing antibiotic classes in ICI patients.\n\n**Constraints Checklist:**\n- JSON object only.\n- Keys: status, material_usefulness, useful_material, auxiliary_material, remaining_gap, outline_action.\n- No quotation ledger, source handles, etc.\n- Refer to paper as 'this study' or 'the authors'.\n- Do not infer identity from reference list.\n- Keep findings attached to study conditions (NSCLC, nivolumab, retrospective).\n- Do not call gap fulfilled if criterion open (need 2 studies).\n\n**Refining Status:**\nThe success criterion is \"Find at least 2 studies...\". This material provides 1 study. Therefore, the criterion is not fully met. Status = \"partial\".\nMaterial Usefulness = \"direct\" (it provides the exact type of data requested: class comparison).\n\n**Useful Material:**\n- Comparison of PTZ vs. Fluoroquinolones vs. Cephalosporins regarding OS/PFS.\n- HR values for specific classes (PTZ HR=3.31 for OS).\n- Duration effects (DOT) per class.\n\n**Auxiliary Material:**\n- Methodology (DOT, DDD).\n- Limitations (sample size for some classes, retrospective, no microbiome data).\n- Population (NSCLC, nivolumab, Korean cohort).\n\n**Remaining Gap:**\n- The success criterion requires 2 studies; only 1 is provided here.\n- Generalizability to other ICIs or cancer types is unconfirmed.\n- \"Safe\" class identification is inconclusive due to small sample sizes for some classes (excluded from analysis if <5).\n\n**Outline Action:**\n- Locate a second study comparing antibiotic classes in ICI treatment.\n- Synthesize findings to determine if PTZ